From: shandike-code <310837749+shandike-code@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:44:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fall back to scontrol when sacct records no job completions

The school cluster runs slurmdbd with the cluster registered but no job
records, so sacct returns empty for every job, past and present. hpc/
supervise.py treated that as "unknown exit" and stopped after ten polls.

Query scontrol first, before the retry loop can outlast the MinJobAge
window, and keep the existing conservative behaviour: a job that is
neither reporting a terminal state nor present in accounting still
raises rather than letting the supervisor resubmit blindly. Record which
source answered in supervisor.json.

Also record the Linux smoke and block-check runs under handoff/linux-runs/
and the frozen Linux environment at environment-linux.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
